**Setup.** Let $g(z)=e^{f(z)}$. Then
$$g''(z)=\bigl(f''(z)+(f'(z))^2\bigr)e^{f(z)},$$
so
$$W:=g''(0)=\bigl(f''(0)+f'(0)^2\bigr)e^{f(0)}.$$

**Parametrization via Schwarz lemma.** Let $A=f(0)$, $|A|\le 1$. Set $\varphi_A(w)=\frac{w-A}{1-\bar A w}$ (automorphism of the disk) and $h=\varphi_A\circ f$. Then $h(0)=0$, $|h(z)|\le 1$, so by Schwarz $h(z)=z\,p(z)$ with $p$ analytic, $|p|\le 1$. Write
$$h(z)=\lambda z+\tfrac{H}{2}z^2+\cdots,\qquad \lambda=h'(0),\; H=h''(0).$$
Then $|\lambda|\le 1$, and $p(0)=\lambda$, $p'(0)=H/2$, so by Schwarz–Pick $|H|\le 2(1-|\lambda|^2)$.

Since $f=\varphi_A^{-1}\circ h$ with $\varphi_A^{-1}(w)=\frac{w+A}{1+\bar A w}$, computing derivatives at $0$:
$$(\varphi_A^{-1})'(0)=1-|A|^2,\qquad (\varphi_A^{-1})''(0)=-2\bar A(1-|A|^2).$$
Hence
$$f'(0)=\lambda(1-|A|^2),\qquad f''(0)=(1-|A|^2)(H-2\bar A\lambda^2),$$
and
$$f''(0)+f'(0)^2=(1-|A|^2)\bigl[H+\lambda^2(1-|A|^2-2\bar A)\bigr].$$

**Universal bound on $|W|$.** Let $r=|A|$, $t=|\lambda|^2$. Then
$$|f''(0)+f'(0)^2|\le(1-r^2)\bigl(|H|+|\lambda|^2\,|1-r^2-2\bar A|\bigr).$$
Using $|H|\le 2(1-t)$ and $|1-r^2-2\bar A|\le(1-r^2)+2r$,
$$|f''(0)+f'(0)^2|\le(1-r^2)\bigl(2(1-t)+t(1-r^2+2r)\bigr)=(1-r^2)\bigl(2-t(1-r)^2\bigr)\le 2(1-r^2).$$
Therefore
$$|W|=e^{\operatorname{Re}A}|f''(0)+f'(0)^2|\le e^r\cdot 2(1-r^2).$$
Maximizing $2e^r(1-r^2)$ on $[0,1]$: the derivative $2e^r(1-r^2-2r)$ vanishes at $r=\sqrt2-1$, giving
$$|W|\le 2e^{\sqrt2-1}\bigl(1-(\sqrt2-1)^2\bigr)=2e^{\sqrt2-1}(2\sqrt2-2)=4(\sqrt2-1)e^{\sqrt2-1}\approx 2.51.$$

